## Architecture

A modular monolith on the TrustOS Engineering Framework. The framework supplies
configuration, authentication, organization-based tenant isolation, RBAC, an
append-only audit trail, structured logging, the error contract, and health
endpoints. This repository supplies the product on top.

```
apps/
{{#if includeApi}}  api/                  NestJS API — product endpoints and auth
{{/if}}{{#if includeAdmin}}  admin/                Next.js admin console
{{/if}}packages/
  product-domain/       product permissions and domain types
  shared-types/         types shared between the API and the admin app
prisma/
  schema/
    00-framework.prisma framework models (copied; do not edit)
    10-product.prisma   product models
docs/                   architecture, deployment and security notes
```

Three global guards run on every request, in this order:

```
JwtAuthGuard       who is calling?          -> request.actor
TenantGuard        whose data may they see? -> request.organizationId
PermissionsGuard   may they do this?        -> deny by default
```

A route that declares no permission is denied. That is deliberate: forgetting a
decorator produces a broken endpoint in staging rather than an open one in
production.

