## Environment variables

| Variable | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `NODE_ENV` | yes | `development`, `test` or `production` |
| `PORT` | yes | API listen port |
| `DATABASE_URL` | yes | PostgreSQL connection string |
| `JWT_SECRET` | yes | 32+ characters in production |
| `JWT_REFRESH_SECRET` | yes | Must differ from `JWT_SECRET` |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | yes | `info` in production |
| `CORS_ORIGINS` | no | Comma-separated; `*` is rejected in production |
| `TRUST_PROXY` | no | `true` behind a load balancer, so audit records get real client IPs |
| `OPENAPI_ENABLED` | no | Serve Swagger at `/docs` |
{{#if includeAdmin}}
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` | no | Admin app only. Compiled into the browser bundle — never a secret. |
{{/if}}

The application refuses to start if a required variable is missing, if a
production secret is shorter than 32 characters, or if the two JWT secrets
match. Every problem is reported at once.

