## Database

```bash
npm run db:migrate -- --name what_changed   # create and apply a migration
npm run db:deploy                            # apply committed migrations
npm run db:seed                              # roles, permissions, dev data
npm run db:validate                          # validate the schema, no database needed
```

Product models go in `prisma/schema/10-product.prisma`. Prisma loads every file
in `prisma/schema/`, so product and framework models compose without either
editing the other. **Do not edit `00-framework.prisma`** — it is replaced when
the framework is upgraded.

---

## Tests and build

```bash
npm test              # unit tests, no database required
npm run typecheck
npm run lint
npm run build
```

The tenant-isolation spec beside the product module is the one that matters
most: a change that makes it fail is a cross-customer data exposure, not a
regression to triage later.

